The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
linked_timeout = io_prep_linked_timeout(req);
if (ret == -EAGAIN && !(req->flags & REQ_F_NOWAIT)) {
    if (io_arm_poll_handler(req)) {
        if (linked_timeout)
            io_queue_linked_timeout(linked_timeout);
        goto exit;
    }
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `io_prep_linked_timeout()` is called, it prepares a linked timeout but does not guarantee that `io_queue_linked_timeout()` is called afterward if the `-EAGAIN` condition is met. This results in linked timeouts being prepared but never queued, leading to inconsistencies in timeout management.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!io_arm_poll_handler(req)) {
    ret = io_prep_work_files(req);
    if (unlikely(ret))
        goto err;
    io_queue_async_work(req);
}
if (linked_timeout)
    io_queue_linked_timeout(linked_timeout);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that `io_queue_linked_timeout(linked_timeout)` is called regardless of whether the poll handler is successful or not. This guarantees that any prepared linked timeouts are queued properly, thus maintaining consistency in timeout management.

